<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<suppressions xmlns="https://jeremylong.github.io/DependencyCheck/dependency-suppression.1.3.xsd">
    <!--
        ========================================================================
        RULE 1: Eclipse Angus Activation - Angus Mail CPE False Positive
        ========================================================================
        Artifact: org.eclipse.angus:angus-activation:2.0.3
        Vulnerability ID: CVE-2025-7962
        Incorrect CPE Assigned by Dependency-Check: cpe:/a:eclipse:angus_mail
        Identification: Verified CPE False Positive
        Date of Verification: 2026-09-29

        Technical Justification:
        1. What the dependency actually is:
           org.eclipse.angus:angus-activation provides the Jakarta Activation Framework
           implementation (MIME type resolution and data handlers).
        2. What product CVE-2025-7962 actually affects:
           CVE-2025-7962 is a vulnerability strictly within the Angus Mail / Jakarta Mail
           SMTP transport implementation (specifically handling malicious multi-line SMTP
           server response sequences).
        3. Why the CPE mapping is incorrect:
           OWASP Dependency-Check mistakenly assigned 'cpe:/a:eclipse:angus_mail' to the
           angus-activation jar because of vendor/group naming similarity. Angus Activation
           contains no mail transport, SMTP protocol handler, or email sending code.
        4. Why the suppression is safe:
           This rule suppresses ONLY the incorrect Angus Mail CPE (cpe:/a:eclipse:angus_mail)
           for org.eclipse.angus:angus-activation. It does NOT suppress by CVE globally, nor
           does it suppress any legitimate Angus Activation CPE or future vulnerabilities
           affecting the Activation library itself.
    -->
    <suppress>
        <notes><![CDATA[
        CPE False Positive: org.eclipse.angus:angus-activation is Jakarta Activation and does not contain
        Angus Mail SMTP transport logic affected by CVE-2025-7962. Verified on 2026-09-29.
        ]]></notes>
        <packageUrl regex="true">^pkg:maven/org\.eclipse\.angus/angus-activation@.*$</packageUrl>
        <cpe>cpe:/a:eclipse:angus_mail</cpe>
    </suppress>

    <!--
        ========================================================================
        RULE 2: Hibernate Validator - Nu Html Checker (validator.nu) CPE False Positive
        ========================================================================
        Artifact: org.hibernate.validator:hibernate-validator:9.1.3.Final
        Vulnerability ID: CVE-2025-15104
        Incorrect CPE Assigned by Dependency-Check: cpe:/a:validator:validator
        Identification: Verified CPE False Positive
        Date of Verification: 2026-09-29

        Technical Justification:
        1. What the dependency actually is:
           org.hibernate.validator:hibernate-validator is the reference implementation
           of Jakarta Bean Validation (Jakarta EE specification for bean validation).
        2. What product CVE-2025-15104 actually affects:
           CVE-2025-15104 is a Server-Side Request Forgery (SSRF) flaw in Nu Html Checker
           (validator.nu / W3C HTML validator service).
        3. Why the CPE mapping is incorrect:
           OWASP Dependency-Check matched the generic keyword 'validator' in the artifact ID
           and assigned 'cpe:/a:validator:validator' (which belongs to validator.nu).
           Hibernate Validator is completely distinct from Nu Html Checker.
        4. Why the suppression is safe:
           This rule suppresses ONLY the erroneous 'cpe:/a:validator:validator' CPE for
           org.hibernate.validator:hibernate-validator. The legitimate CPEs
           (cpe:/a:hibernate:hibernate-validator and cpe:/a:redhat:hibernate_validator)
           remain entirely active and unsuppressed, ensuring that any genuine Hibernate
           Validator vulnerabilities will always be detected.
    -->
    <suppress>
        <notes><![CDATA[
        CPE False Positive: org.hibernate.validator:hibernate-validator is Jakarta Bean Validation and is unrelated
        to the Nu Html Checker (validator.nu) SSRF vulnerability in CVE-2025-15104. Verified on 2026-09-29.
        ]]></notes>
        <packageUrl regex="true">^pkg:maven/org\.hibernate\.validator/hibernate-validator@.*$</packageUrl>
        <cpe>cpe:/a:validator:validator</cpe>
    </suppress>
</suppressions>
